.TH RUNNINGMANAGER 1 "2026-11-05" "RunningManager 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
runningmanager \- lightweight process manager and system monitor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B runningmanager
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B RunningManager
is a desktop process manager and system monitor built with Dear ImGui.
It lists running processes together with their PID, status, user, elevated
privileges, CPU usage and memory usage.
.PP
The process table can be sorted by clicking a column header, filtered with
the search box, and manipulated through the context menu: bring the
application window to the front, open the executable location, or send
SIGKILL to the selected process.
.PP
The left panel shows a system summary with CPU, memory, disk and, when the
driver exposes the required counters, GPU usage.
.SH OPTIONS
The program does not take any command line options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/runningmanager/imgui.ini
Persisted window, table and column layout.  The location follows
.IR XDG_CONFIG_HOME .
.SH NOTES
Bringing a window to the front and detecting GUI processes requires an X11
session with an EWMH-compliant window manager.  On Wayland sessions the
window activation falls back to
.BR xdotool (1)
when it is available.  Opening the executable location requires
.BR xdg-open (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ps (1),
.BR top (1),
.BR kill (1)
